---
description: Python code style
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Python 3.10+, type hints on function signatures, short docstrings (one line).
- Small functions (<30 lines), one job each. Separate: fetching, parsing/transforming, saving, orchestration.
- Use `pathlib.Path`, `with open(..., encoding="utf-8")`, f-strings.
- Never use a mutable default argument (`def f(x=[])`). Use `None` and create inside.
- Never use bare `except:`. Catch specific exceptions; log with `log.exception(...)` when you swallow one.
- No silent failures: if you catch and continue, log it AND record it.
- Use `if __name__ == "__main__":` and `argparse` for the CLI entry point.
- Constants in UPPER_CASE at the top of the module. No magic numbers inline.
- Prefer list/dict comprehensions only when they stay readable.
